<!--
    GH-8777: "PIC24: signed branch lifts to a raw SBORROW flag idiom."
    https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/8777
    Ported from kuna's gh8777-flagcompare-sborrow stage testcase (GayHydra #477).

    In the upstream spec at the time of the issue, "bra ge" was modelled as the
    expanded condition-flag identity
        cond = (SRL_N && SRL_OV) || (!SRL_N && !SRL_OV)        (XNOR(N,V))
    with N = sign of (V - K) and V = INT_SBORROW(V, K).  Upstream has no rule for
    that XNOR tree, so the raw flag algebra survives into the loop condition:

      for (iVar1 = 0; bVar2 = 0 <= iVar1 + -7,
          (bVar2 || !SBORROW2(iVar1,7)) && (!bVar2 || SBORROW2(iVar1,7));
          iVar1 = iVar1 + 1) { ... }

    kuna folds that tree with RuleSborrowGe under "option flagcompare on".

    This fork does NOT reproduce the bug: its PIC24 spec already carries the
    slaspec half of upstream PR #8778 (GayHydra #275), which models "bra ge" as
    the plain  SRL_N == SRL_OV , and the stock RuleSborrow folds that equality
    into the clean signed compare.  Both passes therefore print

      for (iVar1 = 0; iVar1 < 7; iVar1 = iVar1 + 1) {

    RuleSborrowGe is not ported (it would be unreachable here); the option
    "flagcompare" still exists (GH-1276 half) and is toggled as in kuna's script
    so the testcase keeps kuna's shape.  Assert #1: the clean loop header appears
    in both passes.  Assert #2: no SBORROW2 token in either pass.  The stock
    repro of the kuna "bug reproduces" half is recorded above for reference.

    Disassembly:
      0x000000 mov.w #0x0,W2
      0x000002 mov.w #0x7,W3
      0x000004 sub.w W2,W3,W12
      0x000006 bra   ge,0x10
      0x000008 mov.w #0x0,W0
      0x00000a mov.w W0,0x80
      0x00000c add.w W2,#0x1,W2
      0x00000e bra   0x4
      0x000010 return
-->
